  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/574642/diamond-spheres-erudition-esoterica\">Diamond Spheres: Erudition &amp; Esoterica</a></sup></p>\n<p><em>The material that your magic is composed of is naturally volatile once destroyed.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Substantial Magic drawback.</p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Whenever a magic object you have created using the Substantial Magic general drawback is destroyed by a creature, the object releases a burst of magical force, dealing 1d6 + 1d6 bludgeoning damage per 4 caster levels you possess.</p>\n<p>If the sphere effect affected an area, this damage is dealt to all creatures within 5 feet of the magic object (Reflex negates), whereas if the sphere effect affected an individual creature (or otherwise created a worn item), the creature who destroyed the object suffers the damage (Reflex halves).</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/drawback-feats#toc74\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
